        "method": "csv row 53/234 sha256:e054cfc962805b78",
        "content": "# Libriciel SCOP \u2014 (generalist \u2014 see fit)\n\n## Lead record\n- **company**: Libriciel SCOP\n- **tool**: (generalist \u2014 see fit)\n- **priority**: 2 \u00b7 next\n- **geo**: FR\n- **principal**: Matthieu Piaumier, Pr\u00e9sident Directeur G\u00e9n\u00e9ral\n- **email**: contact@libriciel.coop\n- **website**: https://libriciel.fr\n- **tool_url**: \u2014\n- **impressum_url**: https://www.libriciel.fr/mentions-legales/\n- **contact_verified**: Yes\n- **headcount**: \u2014\n- **hq**: \u2014\n- **owner_parent**: \u2014\n- **tech_partners**: \u2014\n- **federation**: \u2014\n- **posture**: \u2014\n- **tier**: \u2014\n- **verdict**: \u2014\n- **flag**: \u2014\n- **source**: \u2014\n- **powerhouse_fit**: iparapheur is an electronic approval circuit for French local government \u2014 it captures signatures but the record lives in a mutable application. For collectivit\u00e9s the question is exactly ours: who approved, under which delegation, and can it be replayed years later.\n- **demo_scenario**: iparapheur approval hook dispatching a typed operation per signature step. Replay a d\u00e9lib\u00e9ration's full approval chain after the workflow has been edited. 90-person SCOP, publishes 12 OSS products.",
